# Alert Rule Monitoring 

This document provides a conceptual overview about alert rules and monitoring for quotas used in the Azure portal. 

Azure quota alert rules are policies customers can configure to be notified and monitor when they are approaching or exceeding their resource usage limits. 

## Alert rules 

Azure quota alerts rules are mechanisms that are created and used by Azure customers to manage their cloud resources, such as storage capacity, and other indicators of performance and usage. 

Alert rules are created, by configuring specific usage scenarios such a set capacity usage of 80%, with frequency of checking every 15 minutes, with conditions to fire a set severity-level alert when this occurs.

When a customer's usage of a particular resource exceeds or approaches the defined threshold, an alert is generated, based on the defined parameters to indicate that the customer is nearing their quota limit.

## Monitor alert rules 

Azure quota alert rule monitoring works by using automated monitoring tools that track usage resource metrics and thresholds specified in the alert rules, that the customer creates based on Azure specifications. These metrics can include usage consumption error rates, and other indicators of performance and usage.

When a metric reaches the threshold defined in an alert rule, such as 80% usage capacity, the monitoring system triggers an alert, which is then sent to the owner or contributor-level users and teams for action. The alert can be delivered by email, SMS, or mobile app with details about the metrics that triggered the alert. Customers can monitor their quotas in real time and can view quota details on Azure quota dashboard. 

Overall, Azure quota alert rule monitoring is essential to manage cloud infrastructure and provides customers with timely alerts and insights into usage trends and anomalies, which allows them to take proactive steps to optimize their resources and avoid or resolve potential issues. 

